          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of a People's Court Not Accepting a Protest Lodged by\na People's Procuratorate Solely in Respect of a Ruling on the Bearing of Litigation Costs\nFa Shi No. 22 [1998]\n(Adopted at the 1,005th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 21 July 1998; promulgated by the Supreme People's Court by announcement on 31 August 1998; coming into force on 5 September 1998)\nthe Higher People's Court of Henan Province:\nThe request for instructions No. 131 [1998] of the Henan Higher People's Court, 'On Whether a Protest Lodged by a People's Procuratorate Solely in Respect of a Ruling on the Bearing of Litigation Costs May Be Accepted', has been received. After study, your court's opinion is agreed to, namely: a protest lodged by a people's procuratorate against a ruling of a people's court on the bearing of litigation costs has no legal basis, and the people's court shall not accept it.\nThis is our reply."
