    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nANNOUNCEMENT\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court 'On the Question of How to Apply the Standard of Compensation for Deprivation of Personal Liberty Where the Compensation Committee of a People's Court, in Accordance with Article 30 of the State Compensation Law of the People's Republic of China, Corrects a Decision of the Compensation Committee That Has Already Taken Effect' was adopted at the 1,621st meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 23 June 2014, and is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 1 August 2014.\n30 June 2014\nSupreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of How to Apply the Standard of Compensation for Deprivation of\nPersonal Liberty Where the Compensation Committee of a People's Court, in Accordance with\nArticle 30 of the State Compensation Law of the People's Republic of China, Corrects a\nDecision of the Compensation Committee That Has Already Taken Effect\nFa Shi No. 7 [2014]\nthe Higher People's Courts of Jilin, Shandong and Henan Provinces:\nWith regard to the question of how the compensation committee of a people's court shall apply the standard of compensation for deprivation of personal liberty in the compensation appeal supervision procedure, after study, the reply is as follows:\nWhere the compensation committee of a people's court, in accordance with Article 30 of the State Compensation Law of the People's Republic of China, corrects a decision of the compensation committee that has already taken effect, and the error in the original decision consists in the omission from the calculation of part of the days of infringement upon personal liberty, the compensation committee shall, while upholding the compensation for deprivation of personal liberty paid under the original decision, calculate, in respect of the omitted days, the corresponding compensation for deprivation of personal liberty according to the standard of the average daily wage of State employees in the previous year at the time the decision is made after re-examination or direct examination; where the error in the original decision consists in the failure to support the claim for compensation for deprivation of personal liberty, the compensation for deprivation of personal liberty shall be calculated according to the standard of the average daily wage of State employees in the previous year at the time the decision is made after re-examination or direct examination."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
      }
    ]
