          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of Whether a People's Court Should Accept a Protest Lodged by a People's Procuratorate\nagainst a Civil Ruling Not to Set Aside an Arbitral Award\nFa Shi No. 46 [2000]\n(Adopted at the 1,150th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 12 December 2000; promulgated by the Supreme People's Court by announcement on 13 December 2000; coming into force on 19 December 2000)\nthe Higher People's Court of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region:\nThe report requesting instructions Nei Fa Min Zai Zi No. 29 [2000] submitted by your court, 'On Whether a People's Procuratorate May Lodge a Protest against a Civil Ruling of a People's Court Not to Set Aside an Arbitral Award', has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nA protest lodged by a people's procuratorate against a civil ruling that has taken legal effect and that does not set aside an arbitral award has no legal basis, and the people's court shall not accept it.\nThis is our reply."
