          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on How to Handle a Suggestion of Suspension of Enforcement\nMade by a People's Procuratorate\nFa Shi No. 16 [2000]\n(Adopted at the 1,121st meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 30 June 2000; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 10 July 2000; coming into force on 15 July 2000)\nTo the Higher People's Court of Guangdong Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court, Yue Gao Fa Min No. 186 [1998], on whether a suggestion of suspension of enforcement made by a procuratorial organ in respect of an effective civil judgment of a court should be adopted, has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nIn accordance with the provisions of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, there is no legal basis for a people's procuratorate to make a suggestion of suspension of enforcement in respect of an effective civil judgment of a people's court.\nThis is our reply."
